1
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:30,560
I think I found a way to get Oab arrested.

2
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:32,400
What can't Oab give you?

3
00:01:32,480 --> 00:01:34,920
He has never gotten involved with drugs.

4
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,200
But if you do,

5
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:39,680
you can get revenge
for your younger brother.

6
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:44,400
- What are you up to?
- I just took him to the foundation.

7
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:45,600
Are you sure?

8
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:50,280
- What does it say?
- A life for a life.

9
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:51,480
A LIFE FOR A LIFE

10
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,200
Hey!

11
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:05,360
Shit.

12
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:09,520
- Fon!
- Fon!

13
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:11,760
- Fon!
- Go to Crime Suppression.

14
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:13,000
Get an ambulance.

15
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:14,640
Now!

16
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:17,080
Fon.

17
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:22,840
Oab, watch out!

18
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:24,520
- Hey!
- Hey! Get out of here!

19
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:34,240
Damn it.

20
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:37,320
Oab!

21
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:39,360
You never watch your back.

22
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:41,880
You knew they were setting you up
to get shot.

23
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:44,320
I didn't see it coming.

24
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:47,840
Exactly. That's why I'm pissed.
You don't care about anything.

25
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:50,080
I'm sorry.

26
00:02:57,360 --> 00:03:00,680
CENTRAL PARK HOSPITAL

27
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:13,400
How are you, Fon?

28
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:16,240
It's just a few scratches.

29
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:19,000
The doctor said it's nothing serious,

30
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:21,560
but he wants me
to stay here for observation.

31
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:25,560
Then get some rest.

32
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:29,480
Okay.

33
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:02,920
She's fine now.

34
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:06,640
I think it was Peng's doing for sure.

35
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:11,680
If there's nothing else,
I'll head back first.

36
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:18,800
That car was stopped at the red light.

37
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:20,440
It only ran it after.

38
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:23,800
Go get some men ready for me.

39
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:26,080
I want you to stay here and keep watch.

40
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:29,760
I don't trust anyone right now.
In case those bastards come back.

41
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:37,360
I told you to take out Oab.

42
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:40,120
You failed,
and you still dare report to me?

43
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:42,000
Pong got in the way.

44
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:43,920
Then you should've killed him too.

45
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:47,120
That would make things complicated.
Right in front of CSD,

46
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:49,040
who would dare?

47
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:50,720
Who would dare?

48
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,240
Liang.

49
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:05,520
What are you doing here?

50
00:05:23,760 --> 00:05:24,960
Are you threatening me?

51
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:30,000
You can call it a threat.

52
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:32,720
But I think you understand.

53
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:35,520
You're keeping Pear hidden from everyone

54
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:37,720
because you're afraid
she'll get caught up in this, right?

55
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:44,120
You think when I begged you last time,

56
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:48,000
- It was because I was afraid of you?
- I know you're not afraid of anyone.

57
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:51,880
I know you're protecting
someone you care about.

58
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:54,600
I have to protect
someone I care about too.

59
00:05:57,480 --> 00:05:58,840
Someone you care about?

60
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:03,800
I thought she was Oab's woman.

61
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,240
Anyone important to Oab

62
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:11,480
is important to me too.

63
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:14,120
Oh.

64
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:17,160
So you're getting worked up for your boss?

65
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:21,520
Just tell me who did it

66
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:23,840
and where they are.

67
00:06:29,280 --> 00:06:30,520
Peng!

68
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:31,960
You wanted me dead, didn't you?

69
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:33,960
Come out. I'm right here!

70
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:36,640
Come out!

71
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,920
Last time you came here,
I didn't kill you.

72
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,120
Are you here to give me another chance?

73
00:07:11,840 --> 00:07:13,360
You sent your men to hurt my girl.

74
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:20,840
What?

75
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:22,520
This is your proof?

76
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:26,040
You're picking a fight with me
over this stupid evidence?

77
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:38,280
Boss, get out of here!

78
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:06,280
Oab.

79
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:11,160
He got away.

80
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:13,600
You need to calm down.

81
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:16,680
How am I supposed to calm down?
Did you see what he did to Fon?

82
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:18,120
I know.

83
00:08:18,840 --> 00:08:22,160
But you need the right timing.
Don't walk in and get yourself killed.

84
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:31,440
If you die today,

85
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:33,799
Arm died for nothing.

86
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:44,920
I thought
Boss was going to kill us for sure.

87
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:48,320
We're lucky he's still giving us a chance.

88
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:51,720
There they are.

89
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:56,440
Let me.

90
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:03,640
Get out of the car.

91
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:06,840
I don't want anyone to see you with me.

92
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:33,760
Champ.

93
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:36,680
We heard there was a shooting
at Peng's karaoke bar.

94
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:40,000
- Has the local station checked it out yet?
- Yes.

95
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:43,640
- Send our people to take a look.
- Yes.

96
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:48,320
Champ.

97
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:50,160
Hey.

98
00:10:51,280 --> 00:10:53,600
What brings Central Investigation to CSD?

99
00:10:58,680 --> 00:10:59,840
My entire team is dead.

100
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:04,160
You don't need to look.

101
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:06,400
You should know without me telling you.

102
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:10,320
Isn't busting drugs your job?

103
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:14,080
How did you let them
operate like this so freely?

104
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:20,800
- Have you issued an arrest warrant?
- Not yet.

105
00:11:22,320 --> 00:11:25,120
We don't know who did it.
How am I supposed to issue a warrant?

106
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:28,080
Whose turf did this happen on?

107
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:31,320
Peng's.

108
00:11:31,920 --> 00:11:34,200
At least you should've talked to him.
See what he says.

109
00:11:38,640 --> 00:11:40,000
There's no evidence.

110
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,640
I don't want trouble
with someone influential.

111
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,320
I don't want problems.

112
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:50,080
Why? Are you afraid of losing your rank?

113
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:57,960
I'm just wondering.

114
00:11:58,560 --> 00:12:01,400
With drugs spreading this badly
in Peng's area, who's behind it?

115
00:12:02,520 --> 00:12:05,320
Why haven't you taken them down?
It's like you're not even trying.

116
00:12:05,400 --> 00:12:06,920
I catch them when I can.

117
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,200
It's not like I do nothing.

118
00:12:13,120 --> 00:12:14,280
Yeah.

119
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:17,080
I don't want you doing this
just for the credit.

120
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:19,520
I want you to do it for the people

121
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:22,080
who have to live in a society
filled with drugs like this.

122
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:26,080
I hope you understand.

123
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:30,000
Today, I came here
as someone who knows you.

124
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:31,880
But if this stays quiet,

125
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:34,640
I'll come back as Central Investigation

126
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:36,280
to investigate you.

127
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:47,720
What happened?

128
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:52,400
Someone hit Fon
to lure Oab out and shoot him.

129
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:55,520
What? I knew it.

130
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:57,680
That's why Pong
gathered everyone at the camp.

131
00:12:57,760 --> 00:13:00,160
- You went with him too, didn't you?
- No.

132
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:03,000
Do you know who he's going after?

133
00:13:03,840 --> 00:13:05,280
If I knew, why would I ask you?

134
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:09,480
Hey.

135
00:13:10,440 --> 00:13:11,440
That's blood.

136
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:13,320
Did Fon get badly hurt?

137
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:15,520
Why is there so much blood?

138
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:17,160
I don't know either.

139
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:19,640
How can you not know?

140
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:21,600
You're the one who should know.

141
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:27,680
Come on.

142
00:14:51,520 --> 00:14:52,680
How are you feeling?

143
00:14:55,880 --> 00:14:57,480
I'm okay.

144
00:14:57,560 --> 00:14:59,200
Don't get up.

145
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:06,680
Did you come alone? What about the others?

146
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:08,760
Pong is waiting outside.

147
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:19,640
What's wrong? Does it hurt a lot?

148
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:27,280
Just rest for now.
Eat when you wake up, okay?

149
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:31,320
I'll cover you.

150
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:47,400
I'll stay here with you.

151
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:06,400
What's wrong, Dom? Tell me.

152
00:16:11,600 --> 00:16:12,920
Hey, Dom.

153
00:16:13,800 --> 00:16:15,360
I know everything about you.

154
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:17,080
You don't have to hide from me.

155
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:22,280
I did something I never thought I'd do.

156
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:24,680
What did you do?

157
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:28,120
I killed someone.

158
00:16:32,240 --> 00:16:35,200
Hey, you were just trying to survive.

159
00:16:36,440 --> 00:16:40,320
It was either him or you.
Don't overthink it, Bro.

160
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,480
I killed someone

161
00:16:44,160 --> 00:16:46,520
and I enjoyed seeing them die.

162
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:09,160
Hello?

163
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:11,680
Mom.

164
00:17:16,760 --> 00:17:17,839
I'm sorry.

165
00:17:18,599 --> 00:17:20,200
TELEPHONE

166
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:22,200
I'm sorry I couldn't keep her safe.

167
00:17:31,520 --> 00:17:33,160
I'm sorry.

168
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:52,360
Honey, I'm going to Bangkok
to see our daughter.

169
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:56,680
She was hit by a car
and she's in the hospital, but she's safe.

170
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:59,240
I'll stay with her for a few days.

171
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:07,640
Oab, go home and rest.
You'll sleep better there.

172
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:10,320
I'll stay here.

173
00:18:11,120 --> 00:18:12,600
I wouldn't be able to sleep
at home anyway.

174
00:18:20,640 --> 00:18:22,320
Are you uncomfortable with me here?

175
00:18:26,960 --> 00:18:27,960
I just feel bad.

176
00:18:28,920 --> 00:18:30,520
Don't worry about it.

177
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:33,720
I'll sleep better here than at home.

178
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:55,200
Don't worry, I won't do anything to you.

179
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:10,360
- Call me if you need anything.
- Okay.

180
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:18,840
Hey, Oab.

181
00:19:20,480 --> 00:19:22,520
Why did you go to CSD this morning?

182
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:25,440
I was worried.

183
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:28,880
You suddenly got worried?

184
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:34,280
Get some sleep.

185
00:20:04,360 --> 00:20:05,400
Pong.

186
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:13,000
Go home, take a shower, and get some rest.
I'll stay here.

187
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:14,360
No need.

188
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:17,120
Come on. I can handle it.

189
00:20:23,560 --> 00:20:27,560
Are you staying because
you don't trust me or don't like me?

190
00:20:27,640 --> 00:20:28,920
Both.

191
00:20:31,760 --> 00:20:33,000
Fine, suit yourself.

192
00:20:34,360 --> 00:20:36,840
- Pong.
- Yeah?

193
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,920
I called Oab's house, but no one answered.

194
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:43,560
So I called the camp.
They said you guys were here. Where's Oab?

195
00:20:44,440 --> 00:20:45,560
He's inside. Wait.

196
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:47,480
Hey, Pom!

197
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:50,480
Oab.

198
00:20:53,240 --> 00:20:54,120
Oh.

199
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:00,360
Pong.

200
00:21:01,360 --> 00:21:03,760
- Oab's not hurt.
- I was about to tell you.

201
00:21:04,920 --> 00:21:07,640
Then who's that woman?

202
00:21:07,720 --> 00:21:10,320
- His girlfriend.
- Girlfriend?

203
00:21:11,040 --> 00:21:12,680
I leave him alone
and he gets a girlfriend?

204
00:21:20,600 --> 00:21:23,240
Well? Who is she?

205
00:21:30,600 --> 00:21:32,920
If I hadn't seen it myself,
would you have told me?

206
00:21:33,440 --> 00:21:34,720
I want to be her boyfriend.

207
00:21:36,520 --> 00:21:37,560
I don't know if she feels the same.

208
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:42,320
- What's wrong?
- Why did you come looking for me?

209
00:21:43,840 --> 00:21:44,800
There's a problem.

210
00:21:46,840 --> 00:21:48,200
Is it about me?

211
00:21:49,080 --> 00:21:50,480
Yeah.

212
00:21:55,160 --> 00:21:56,160
I'm asking for real.

213
00:21:58,920 --> 00:22:00,200
I'm asking you as a friend.

214
00:22:05,040 --> 00:22:06,360
Are you guys selling drugs?

215
00:22:09,480 --> 00:22:10,320
No.

216
00:22:14,320 --> 00:22:15,680
Then look at this case.

217
00:22:22,120 --> 00:22:23,080
POLICE RECORDS DIVISION

218
00:22:23,160 --> 00:22:24,520
My undercover team is all dead.

219
00:22:27,360 --> 00:22:29,520
POLICE RECORDS DIVISION - HOMICIDE CASE

220
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:37,720
- You know him?
- Yeah.

221
00:22:38,520 --> 00:22:39,840
He's one of mine.

222
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:42,920
These two cases
happened in different areas.

223
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:45,360
My undercover officer
died in Peng's territory.

224
00:22:46,760 --> 00:22:48,880
But this guy died in your area.

225
00:22:51,840 --> 00:22:54,760
- So?
- I found drugs on him

226
00:22:55,400 --> 00:22:57,160
that were clearly not for personal use.

227
00:22:58,920 --> 00:23:01,200
That means someone
is selling drugs in your area.

228
00:23:05,120 --> 00:23:06,640
Peng's men did it.

229
00:23:09,800 --> 00:23:11,040
How do you know?

230
00:23:11,120 --> 00:23:14,560
They sent someone to threaten us,
so I rushed to you.

231
00:23:15,360 --> 00:23:16,800
Luckily, I made it in time.

232
00:23:18,920 --> 00:23:20,560
That's how people with power are.

233
00:23:21,360 --> 00:23:23,680
They keep taking revenge on each other.

234
00:23:24,320 --> 00:23:28,360
Honestly, it won't end until someone dies.

235
00:24:11,400 --> 00:24:12,800
I came to get the tray.

236
00:24:25,040 --> 00:24:25,840
‪Dom,

237
00:24:30,200 --> 00:24:33,400
take over here. Let Pong go home and rest.

238
00:24:34,200 --> 00:24:35,080
Yes.

239
00:24:39,840 --> 00:24:41,200
Let's go.

240
00:24:53,120 --> 00:24:54,600
I need to talk to you

241
00:24:55,560 --> 00:24:57,040
about what you asked me the other day.

242
00:25:00,360 --> 00:25:03,480
We found them dead outside the house.
Looks like it happened last night.

243
00:25:03,560 --> 00:25:05,120
Oab's men probably did it.

244
00:25:14,640 --> 00:25:16,520
If he could come straight to me,

245
00:25:17,360 --> 00:25:19,160
he wouldn't leave the others alone.

246
00:25:21,800 --> 00:25:25,080
This whole mess makes me look weak.

247
00:25:28,400 --> 00:25:31,040
And I don't like losing face.

248
00:25:47,360 --> 00:25:49,920
Oab, do you still have to think about it?

249
00:25:54,440 --> 00:25:56,440
Even now, I still don't want to do it.

250
00:26:02,760 --> 00:26:04,440
If that's your decision,

251
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:06,240
then fine.

252
00:26:16,880 --> 00:26:17,960
Then go tell him

253
00:26:19,360 --> 00:26:20,320
I agree.

254
00:26:22,400 --> 00:26:24,560
But I want to discuss the terms first.

255
00:26:28,120 --> 00:26:29,800
Have him set a time and place.

256
00:26:42,520 --> 00:26:45,080
It's good, isn't it?
That's why you came back.

257
00:26:45,680 --> 00:26:46,400
Yes.

258
00:26:47,440 --> 00:26:50,320
Then I'll pack some for you to take home.

259
00:26:50,920 --> 00:26:52,120
Thank you.

260
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:10,880
He agreed?

261
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:12,600
Yes.

262
00:27:17,080 --> 00:27:18,280
But there's a condition.

263
00:27:20,120 --> 00:27:22,680
- What is it?
- I don't know.

264
00:27:24,040 --> 00:27:25,360
He said he wants to talk to you himself.

265
00:27:29,200 --> 00:27:32,960
But you can choose the time and place.

266
00:27:37,360 --> 00:27:40,600
I'll meet him alone. No men with him.

267
00:27:47,920 --> 00:27:51,560
I'll call the number you gave me
with the time and place.

268
00:27:54,240 --> 00:27:55,560
Are you done?

269
00:27:55,640 --> 00:27:57,560
- Need any help?
- Here.

270
00:27:57,640 --> 00:27:59,040
I already packed it.

271
00:28:00,680 --> 00:28:02,600
Okay. This one's the takeaway order.

272
00:28:06,120 --> 00:28:07,840
The wound looks much better.

273
00:28:07,920 --> 00:28:09,600
When will the doctor let me go home?

274
00:28:10,200 --> 00:28:12,600
The doctor will come check on you soon.
You can ask then.

275
00:28:17,200 --> 00:28:18,560
Getting tired of the hospital?

276
00:28:21,440 --> 00:28:23,320
All I do here is sit around and rest.

277
00:28:23,400 --> 00:28:26,200
I still haven't told Mom.

278
00:28:26,840 --> 00:28:29,080
She's probably been calling nonstop.

279
00:28:31,400 --> 00:28:32,400
- Hello.
- Mom.

280
00:28:32,480 --> 00:28:33,840
Hi, Dear.

281
00:28:35,440 --> 00:28:37,720
Why didn't you tell me?

282
00:28:38,920 --> 00:28:40,280
You too, Oab.

283
00:28:41,200 --> 00:28:43,040
You should've told me.

284
00:28:43,120 --> 00:28:46,040
Why are you two acting like kids?

285
00:28:46,800 --> 00:28:49,080
I'm fine now.

286
00:28:50,120 --> 00:28:52,280
I miss you so much.

287
00:28:54,560 --> 00:28:58,200
I miss you too.
And I've been so worried about you.

288
00:28:58,280 --> 00:29:00,120
I'm not hurt at all.

289
00:29:01,360 --> 00:29:02,960
Don't even say that.

290
00:29:03,040 --> 00:29:03,960
Oh my.

291
00:29:04,600 --> 00:29:07,080
Did Dad come too?

292
00:29:07,920 --> 00:29:09,720
He was going to come,

293
00:29:09,800 --> 00:29:12,800
but a senior official came from Bangkok,
so he had to stay.

294
00:29:13,960 --> 00:29:17,520
That's why I'm here
to give you an earful from him.

295
00:29:17,600 --> 00:29:20,160
Or do you want him
to come scold you himself?

296
00:29:21,440 --> 00:29:22,280
No way.

297
00:29:22,360 --> 00:29:24,280
You coming alone is enough.

298
00:29:35,200 --> 00:29:36,320
What do you need, Oab?

299
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:38,840
Nothing. Fon's mom came,

300
00:29:39,480 --> 00:29:40,680
so I stepped outside.

301
00:29:41,560 --> 00:29:44,760
She really scolded me
for not telling her Fon got hit by a car.

302
00:29:53,160 --> 00:29:54,280
How did it go?

303
00:29:59,840 --> 00:30:02,680
He said he'll call
to set the time and place.

304
00:30:03,720 --> 00:30:04,720
Good.

305
00:30:30,120 --> 00:30:31,480
Took you long enough.

306
00:30:33,040 --> 00:30:35,040
I had to wait until everyone was asleep.

307
00:30:37,640 --> 00:30:40,760
- Still haven't found anything?
- No.

308
00:30:42,360 --> 00:30:44,480
We've got dead drug dealers in your area.

309
00:30:45,320 --> 00:30:46,680
And you said Oab wasn't selling?

310
00:30:52,880 --> 00:30:54,080
I don't know these four.

311
00:30:57,360 --> 00:30:58,320
They were undercover.

312
00:31:00,880 --> 00:31:02,240
What about this guy?

313
00:31:03,600 --> 00:31:06,080
CASE NO. 137/31

314
00:31:09,320 --> 00:31:11,360
You know where he died.

315
00:31:15,120 --> 00:31:19,040
Oab's own man
is selling drugs in his territory.

316
00:31:19,640 --> 00:31:21,240
And you're telling me he knew nothing?

317
00:31:22,400 --> 00:31:25,200
I don't believe
he has nothing to do with it.

318
00:31:30,440 --> 00:31:33,920
Stop denying it and find me some evidence.

319
00:32:02,520 --> 00:32:03,560
Pong.

320
00:32:08,480 --> 00:32:12,720
If anything changes,
I want you to take over for me.

321
00:32:14,440 --> 00:32:15,840
What are you talking about?

322
00:32:19,360 --> 00:32:21,240
Once I deal with Peng,

323
00:32:21,320 --> 00:32:24,520
I think I want to walk away.

324
00:32:33,400 --> 00:32:34,760
People like us

325
00:32:36,120 --> 00:32:37,600
can't just walk away.

326
00:32:42,880 --> 00:32:44,640
Once you're on top,

327
00:32:46,080 --> 00:32:48,040
you can't just step down.

328
00:32:49,800 --> 00:32:51,760
People are waiting to destroy you.

329
00:32:53,000 --> 00:32:57,240
And I don't want to see them
tear you apart.

330
00:33:03,800 --> 00:33:05,560
There has to be a way.

331
00:33:44,640 --> 00:33:46,200
Dom.

332
00:33:46,280 --> 00:33:48,480
- Mom.
- Dom.

333
00:33:48,560 --> 00:33:50,040
You came here secretly, didn't you?

334
00:33:50,120 --> 00:33:52,120
Yeah. I was worried.

335
00:33:53,440 --> 00:33:55,760
If they come after you,
what are you going to do?

336
00:34:01,960 --> 00:34:03,080
Dom.

337
00:34:04,480 --> 00:34:06,520
Do you remember
what the elder monk taught you?

338
00:34:09,560 --> 00:34:10,760
About what?

339
00:34:11,480 --> 00:34:14,600
A grudge ends when you stop holding one.

340
00:34:17,520 --> 00:34:20,880
Whatever you can let go of now, do it.

341
00:34:23,600 --> 00:34:27,880
Don't chase after things
beyond your reach.

342
00:34:27,960 --> 00:34:29,239
Stepping back now

343
00:34:30,040 --> 00:34:33,960
may be better than chasing them
until you can't turn back anymore.

344
00:34:37,800 --> 00:34:39,239
If I step back now,

345
00:34:40,440 --> 00:34:42,560
I'll never be good enough for Fon

346
00:34:43,800 --> 00:34:45,600
in her father's eyes.

347
00:34:46,600 --> 00:34:47,800
Dom.

348
00:34:48,560 --> 00:34:51,159
You don't have to be good enough
for anyone.

349
00:34:52,360 --> 00:34:54,320
Just be good to Fon

350
00:34:54,400 --> 00:34:56,520
and make her happy.

351
00:34:57,160 --> 00:34:59,760
I think that's enough.

352
00:35:00,680 --> 00:35:03,360
As for Dad, let him say what he wants.

353
00:35:03,440 --> 00:35:06,320
If we haven't done anything
to hurt anyone,

354
00:35:06,400 --> 00:35:10,200
shouldn't we just live our lives
and be happy?

355
00:35:40,040 --> 00:35:41,080
Hello?

356
00:35:45,480 --> 00:35:46,480
What is it?

357
00:35:51,080 --> 00:35:52,080
Yeah, okay.

358
00:35:54,600 --> 00:35:57,960
Pong, go to the hospital
and bring Fon and her mom home for me.

359
00:35:59,000 --> 00:36:00,040
Fon called?

360
00:36:00,920 --> 00:36:03,520
Where are you going?

361
00:36:05,240 --> 00:36:06,440
Dom, drive for me.

362
00:36:24,680 --> 00:36:26,160
Wait here.

363
00:36:53,280 --> 00:36:55,840
You're really willing to become
what you've always hated?

364
00:37:01,160 --> 00:37:02,040
Yes.

365
00:37:02,800 --> 00:37:05,080
Just to get me to point you to him?

366
00:37:08,480 --> 00:37:09,640
You can do that, right?

367
00:37:14,560 --> 00:37:19,200
That depends
on whether I can accept your offer.

368
00:37:24,480 --> 00:37:26,520
I'll let you sell
in Peng's territory only.

369
00:37:27,560 --> 00:37:28,920
What do you mean?

370
00:37:32,000 --> 00:37:33,520
If I take him out,

371
00:37:34,160 --> 00:37:36,280
I'll give you control of his territory.

372
00:37:37,280 --> 00:37:38,680
As for the drugs,

373
00:37:38,760 --> 00:37:41,840
you sell only in Peng's territory.
Don't sell in mine.

374
00:37:47,160 --> 00:37:49,000
You're giving me his territory?

375
00:37:50,840 --> 00:37:55,720
We split your profits fifty-fifty.
I won't touch the drug money.

376
00:37:56,560 --> 00:37:58,040
Whatever you make, you keep.

377
00:38:03,280 --> 00:38:04,360
Deal.

378
00:38:08,120 --> 00:38:09,280
Let me know when you're ready.

379
00:38:12,880 --> 00:38:13,800
Wait.

380
00:38:16,560 --> 00:38:18,440
Who ran over my woman?

381
00:38:20,920 --> 00:38:22,680
I thought Dom already handled it for you.

382
00:38:26,280 --> 00:38:27,640
He didn't tell you?

383
00:38:56,920 --> 00:38:57,800
What's wrong, Oab?

384
00:39:03,400 --> 00:39:04,840
Who ran her over?

385
00:39:11,600 --> 00:39:13,040
Peng's men.

386
00:39:14,160 --> 00:39:16,040
They meant to kill her.

387
00:39:43,800 --> 00:39:45,240
You took care of them already, right?

388
00:39:49,120 --> 00:39:49,920
Yes.

389
00:39:57,600 --> 00:39:58,440
Thanks.

390
00:40:12,240 --> 00:40:14,960
Oab seems to take good care of you too.

391
00:40:15,680 --> 00:40:16,760
Yes, Mom.

392
00:40:17,280 --> 00:40:20,640
Even when he's not around,
he still has his guy drive you home.

393
00:40:38,080 --> 00:40:40,080
Do you feel anything for Oab?

394
00:40:44,520 --> 00:40:45,320
Even a little?

395
00:40:48,880 --> 00:40:49,800
No, not at all.

396
00:40:50,920 --> 00:40:55,080
We're close,
but he's just like an older brother to me.

397
00:40:56,240 --> 00:40:58,560
If that's how it is, then I'm relieved.

398
00:41:14,600 --> 00:41:15,720
Come in.

399
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:25,520
Oh, perfect timing.

400
00:41:25,600 --> 00:41:26,640
Hi, Dear.

401
00:41:26,720 --> 00:41:29,480
I was going to buy
some groceries to make dinner.

402
00:41:30,120 --> 00:41:31,440
Oab.

403
00:41:31,520 --> 00:41:34,760
Could you have Dom help me carry
some bags from the market?

404
00:41:36,600 --> 00:41:38,080
I'll take you myself.

405
00:41:38,160 --> 00:41:39,880
The market is just nearby.

406
00:41:40,920 --> 00:41:43,200
You just sit there.

407
00:41:43,280 --> 00:41:45,400
Once you're better,
you can go back to work.

408
00:41:46,880 --> 00:41:47,680
Dom, let's go.

409
00:41:48,800 --> 00:41:49,760
Go ahead.

410
00:41:51,040 --> 00:41:52,200
Yes.

411
00:41:57,840 --> 00:42:00,400
Is it tough living at the camp?

412
00:42:00,480 --> 00:42:02,120
Why do you ask, Mom?

413
00:42:02,720 --> 00:42:05,080
Just look at you.

414
00:42:05,600 --> 00:42:07,040
You've gotten so skinny.

415
00:42:07,840 --> 00:42:08,920
I've been training too much.

416
00:42:11,040 --> 00:42:13,200
- Mom!
- Oh!

417
00:42:17,800 --> 00:42:18,800
Hey!

418
00:42:18,880 --> 00:42:20,360
He was probably in a hurry.

419
00:42:20,440 --> 00:42:23,920
That's exactly how they made it look
when Fon got hit by the car.

420
00:42:25,440 --> 00:42:28,320
It's okay. It's probably nothing.

421
00:42:29,160 --> 00:42:31,320
Come on, let's go.

422
00:42:40,640 --> 00:42:42,080
Have you eaten yet?

423
00:42:42,160 --> 00:42:44,720
- Not yet, Mom.
- Come on in.

424
00:42:44,800 --> 00:42:48,080
Two plates of rice,
Kaeng Som, and an omelet.

425
00:42:48,160 --> 00:42:50,000
- Have a seat.
- Come on, let's sit down.

426
00:42:52,960 --> 00:42:54,240
Thank you.

427
00:43:09,080 --> 00:43:12,600
Whenever I make Kaeng Som at home,
I always think of you.

428
00:43:14,680 --> 00:43:16,640
I don't really buy food here.

429
00:43:16,720 --> 00:43:20,720
I eat whatever they make at the camp.
I have to pay for anything else.

430
00:43:22,520 --> 00:43:23,840
Then eat up.

431
00:43:39,960 --> 00:43:41,800
I think you've changed, Dom.

432
00:43:43,120 --> 00:43:46,440
You used to be calmer.

433
00:43:49,760 --> 00:43:51,800
I like that you're kind,

434
00:43:52,600 --> 00:43:54,960
that you take care of Fon,

435
00:43:55,560 --> 00:43:59,920
and that you stay calm
and handle problems well.

436
00:44:01,320 --> 00:44:04,640
Don't let anyone or anything change you.

437
00:44:09,640 --> 00:44:10,840
Yes, Mom.

438
00:44:12,600 --> 00:44:14,600
When we're not around anymore,

439
00:44:15,480 --> 00:44:16,880
you'll be the one

440
00:44:17,720 --> 00:44:20,480
taking care of Fon
for the rest of her life.

441
00:44:33,560 --> 00:44:34,840
Keep eating.

442
00:44:49,840 --> 00:44:51,080
Hey, Liang.

443
00:44:51,680 --> 00:44:53,120
Yes, Boss.

444
00:44:53,840 --> 00:44:57,680
Man's been getting difficult lately.
I went to the boxing camp,

445
00:44:58,320 --> 00:45:00,360
and he demanded a bigger cut.

446
00:45:01,640 --> 00:45:04,280
- You're basically taking care of him.
- Exactly.

447
00:45:04,880 --> 00:45:05,880
Fifty-fifty.

448
00:45:05,960 --> 00:45:07,720
His fifty goes straight into his pocket,

449
00:45:07,800 --> 00:45:10,720
while my fifty has to cover
his food, water, electricity,

450
00:45:10,800 --> 00:45:12,240
and medical bills.

451
00:45:13,000 --> 00:45:14,800
What did you tell him?

452
00:45:14,880 --> 00:45:16,640
I told him I'd think about it.

453
00:45:16,720 --> 00:45:18,200
I think

454
00:45:19,200 --> 00:45:21,840
I'll just sell Man to another camp
and be done with it.

455
00:45:21,920 --> 00:45:24,640
I'll meet them the day after tomorrow
in Phutthamonthon.

456
00:45:25,640 --> 00:45:27,000
Go with me.

457
00:45:28,880 --> 00:45:31,360
- What time?
- Around 7 or 8 p.m.

458
00:45:33,120 --> 00:45:34,400
Yes.

459
00:45:37,760 --> 00:45:40,920
I've hired professionals
to take care of Oab's woman.

460
00:45:41,760 --> 00:45:43,440
This time,

461
00:45:43,520 --> 00:45:44,760
it'll be taken care of.

462
00:46:06,680 --> 00:46:08,880
Who is it? They won't stop calling.

463
00:46:08,960 --> 00:46:10,680
What should we do? It keeps ringing.

464
00:46:11,200 --> 00:46:12,360
Should we answer it?

465
00:46:12,440 --> 00:46:13,720
Try answering. Go ahead.

466
00:46:15,080 --> 00:46:18,640
Wait, how am I supposed to answer it?

467
00:46:23,200 --> 00:46:24,320
What are you guys doing?

468
00:46:25,040 --> 00:46:27,320
I don't know who it is.
They've been calling nonstop.

469
00:46:27,400 --> 00:46:28,560
Yeah.

470
00:46:37,240 --> 00:46:38,200
Hello?

471
00:46:49,280 --> 00:46:50,200
Too late.

472
00:46:50,920 --> 00:46:53,760
What? It's been ringing for minutes.

473
00:46:53,840 --> 00:46:55,320
Who is it?

474
00:47:11,040 --> 00:47:12,480
Why is Mom taking so long?

475
00:47:13,800 --> 00:47:16,680
- I'll go check on her.
- I'll go with you.

476
00:47:23,800 --> 00:47:26,320
Oh, I almost forgot.

477
00:47:26,400 --> 00:47:29,000
Once we go upstairs,
I won't be able to give this to you.

478
00:47:38,400 --> 00:47:39,280
Here.

479
00:47:42,440 --> 00:47:45,000
May this Buddha amulet protect you.

480
00:47:45,760 --> 00:47:49,320
May you stay safe from all harm

481
00:47:50,000 --> 00:47:54,440
and have the happy family life
you've always dreamed of, Dear.

482
00:48:15,120 --> 00:48:17,480
Wow, Mom. You bought so much.

483
00:48:17,560 --> 00:48:19,800
She said she was going to cook for us.

484
00:48:19,880 --> 00:48:21,480
Oh, okay.

485
00:48:21,560 --> 00:48:23,560
Let's do it at the camp.
We'll have help there.

486
00:48:23,640 --> 00:48:26,360
That's a good idea.
Fon can get out of the room for a bit too.

487
00:48:26,440 --> 00:48:27,480
Shall we go?

488
00:48:28,080 --> 00:48:29,040
- Come on.
- Yes.

489
00:49:16,960 --> 00:49:18,840
Stop!

490
00:49:19,440 --> 00:49:21,120
- Let him go!
- Drop the gun!

491
00:49:22,400 --> 00:49:23,600
Slowly get up.

492
00:49:24,920 --> 00:49:26,120
- Do it!
- Put the gun down.

493
00:49:27,880 --> 00:49:29,040
Slowly get up.

494
00:49:29,720 --> 00:49:30,880
Hands behind your head.

495
00:49:56,000 --> 00:49:58,920
- No, Mom!
- Mom!

496
00:49:59,000 --> 00:50:00,640
Mom, wake up.

497
00:50:00,720 --> 00:50:02,240
Mom.

498
00:50:03,600 --> 00:50:04,960
Mom, wake up.

499
00:50:05,040 --> 00:50:07,280
Mom!

500
00:50:09,520 --> 00:50:11,000
Mom!

501
00:50:12,400 --> 00:50:16,480
No, Mom!

502
00:50:21,640 --> 00:50:23,000
Mom.

503
00:50:48,880 --> 00:50:50,560
We can collect her body tomorrow.

504
00:51:09,520 --> 00:51:11,120
It has to be Peng.

505
00:51:13,440 --> 00:51:14,640
Please stop, Dom.

506
00:51:15,840 --> 00:51:17,760
Can we end this here?

507
00:51:52,720 --> 00:51:55,120
I talked to him already.
He'll take care of it.

508
00:52:04,680 --> 00:52:06,960
Hey, you've got some serious connections.

509
00:52:07,040 --> 00:52:08,960
I got a call
saying someone got him released.

510
00:52:09,920 --> 00:52:11,400
Who the hell was it?

511
00:52:12,240 --> 00:52:15,600
- He didn't tell you who it was?
- He said he didn't want to get in trouble.

512
00:52:17,800 --> 00:52:19,320
It must be someone powerful.

513
00:52:19,400 --> 00:52:21,440
I think Oab
is getting more dangerous every day.

514
00:52:21,520 --> 00:52:23,480
If I don't cut him off
before he grows stronger,

515
00:52:23,560 --> 00:52:25,760
he'll end up stepping over me for real.

516
00:52:41,800 --> 00:52:43,520
I asked you guys to keep things quiet.

517
00:52:44,320 --> 00:52:47,240
You call shooting someone in the city
keeping things quiet?

518
00:52:47,320 --> 00:52:48,480
I was defending myself.

519
00:52:48,560 --> 00:52:50,400
We have the police to catch criminals.

520
00:52:50,480 --> 00:52:51,800
You don't have to do it.

521
00:52:53,000 --> 00:52:54,440
If I waited, they'd never be caught.

522
00:52:55,400 --> 00:52:57,680
But you can't just pull out a gun
and shoot.

523
00:52:57,760 --> 00:52:59,400
It's a crowded area.

524
00:52:59,480 --> 00:53:02,160
If civilians got caught in the crossfire,
who would take responsibility?

525
00:53:02,240 --> 00:53:03,600
Come on, Sir.

526
00:53:04,240 --> 00:53:06,120
No one got hurt, we caught them,

527
00:53:06,200 --> 00:53:08,560
and Oab won't go to jail.
It shouldn't be a problem.

528
00:53:08,640 --> 00:53:12,360
But I'm the one
putting my neck on the line.

529
00:53:12,440 --> 00:53:14,080
I could lose my job over this.

530
00:53:14,680 --> 00:53:17,720
How about this? I'm sorry.

531
00:53:17,800 --> 00:53:19,120
It was an emergency.

532
00:53:23,040 --> 00:53:27,040
I'm asking you guys
to stay quiet for a while.

533
00:53:27,120 --> 00:53:28,880
I don't want
the higher-ups looking into this.

534
00:53:28,960 --> 00:53:31,240
And if I can't even ask you for that,

535
00:53:31,920 --> 00:53:34,640
then you and I can't work together.

536
00:53:34,720 --> 00:53:36,760
I'll try my best.

537
00:53:38,080 --> 00:53:40,160
I'll get going. Goodbye. Come on, Pong.

538
00:53:46,440 --> 00:53:48,280
Go back and prepare a room for me.

539
00:53:48,360 --> 00:53:49,840
What? Who's going to stay--

540
00:54:01,720 --> 00:54:04,920
After the funeral, we'll tell the chief

541
00:54:05,800 --> 00:54:07,080
that we're quitting.

542
00:54:23,680 --> 00:54:24,880
Thank you.

543
00:54:25,800 --> 00:54:27,440
MORTUARY

544
00:54:35,720 --> 00:54:37,960
Have they told you
when you can collect her body?

545
00:54:48,920 --> 00:54:50,200
Tomorrow.

546
00:54:58,520 --> 00:54:59,520
I'm sorry.

547
00:55:02,760 --> 00:55:05,440
I'm sorry this all happened to you
because of me.

548
00:55:09,320 --> 00:55:10,880
You don't have to apologize.

549
00:55:11,520 --> 00:55:12,920
It wasn't your fault.

550
00:55:15,240 --> 00:55:17,280
It wasn't anyone's fault

551
00:55:17,800 --> 00:55:19,120
except whoever ordered it.

552
00:55:22,960 --> 00:55:25,120
What did my mom ever do to deserve this?

553
00:55:35,720 --> 00:55:37,680
Have you followed up on the case?

554
00:55:39,880 --> 00:55:42,160
Champ is handling it.

555
00:55:43,880 --> 00:55:45,200
He's probably investigating.

556
00:55:50,000 --> 00:55:53,200
We'll know who did this soon, Fon.

557
00:56:37,560 --> 00:56:40,440
Hey, why aren't you answering?

558
00:56:49,320 --> 00:56:50,760
You guys were arrested

559
00:56:51,800 --> 00:56:53,280
for murder.

560
00:56:55,040 --> 00:56:56,840
Aren't you going to name names?

561
00:56:58,160 --> 00:57:00,440
- No.
- Are you sure?

562
00:57:00,520 --> 00:57:02,560
Yeah, I'm sure.

563
00:57:05,800 --> 00:57:06,920
Good.

564
00:57:17,840 --> 00:57:22,640
If you can do what you say,
you'll be out sooner than you think.

565
00:57:36,160 --> 00:57:37,480
I'm sorry, Dad.

566
00:57:42,520 --> 00:57:46,680
I promise I'll take responsibility
for what happened to your mom

567
00:57:46,760 --> 00:57:48,400
and your family.

568
00:57:49,960 --> 00:57:51,080
Mom.

569
00:57:53,160 --> 00:57:54,720
I shouldn't have chosen this path.

570
00:57:55,920 --> 00:57:57,280
I'm sorry about your mom.

571
00:57:57,360 --> 00:58:00,200
But they confirmed the same thing
I told you the other day.

572
00:58:00,280 --> 00:58:01,920
They're lying.

573
00:58:02,000 --> 00:58:04,640
- Aren't you going to keep investigating?
- How can I?

574
00:58:05,160 --> 00:58:06,520
They refuse to implicate anyone.

575
00:58:06,600 --> 00:58:08,640
I think I should go back to Khon Kaen.

576
00:58:09,240 --> 00:58:10,200
Why?

577
00:58:10,280 --> 00:58:11,680
Lately,

578
00:58:12,600 --> 00:58:14,720
I've held a gun
more than I've worn boxing gloves.

579
00:58:14,800 --> 00:58:16,440
Are you taking the bag too?

580
00:58:16,520 --> 00:58:17,440
It's Fon's.

581
00:58:18,520 --> 00:58:19,920
I asked her to stay at my house.

582
00:58:20,560 --> 00:58:21,840
It's safer this way.

583
00:58:55,240 --> 00:58:56,160
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
